IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 4, Division 7 -- Title and transfers, private companies: transfer of shares and debentures, registration at the transferor's request, notice of refusal (ss 126 to 129; s 128A repealed). Layer 1, part agent sgj.
-- Source file lines 10604-10750. The text is a rendering of the Act, not the official text.
-- HOW IT IS MODELLED: as in sgj-div5-debentures.l4. Taken as a fact from another part (PLAN.md section 4): `the company is a private company` (s 4(1) "private company"), and
-- `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)` (s 196A, part sgm).
-- The clock of the traces counts days after the event named in each rule.

§ `Section 126: transfer of shares in private companies`

DECLARE `s 126 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 126(1) lodge a transfer of shares without a proper instrument of transfer having been delivered to the company`
    `s 126(2) lodge with the Registrar notice of the transfer of shares in the prescribed form`

-- s 126(1): a private company must not lodge a transfer of shares unless a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered; this does not affect the power to lodge a notice of transfer on a transmission by operation of law.
-- A bar: JUST TRUE means the company is barred. The bar is closed by its own "unless" and its own carve-out, which are the text's no; a company that is not private is not covered.
-- src:10606 | 126.—(1) Despite anything in its constitution, a private company
-- src:10607 | must not lodge a transfer of shares unless a proper instrument of
-- src:10608 | transfer has been delivered to the company, but this section does not
-- src:10609 | affect any power to lodge a notice of transfer of shares in respect of
-- src:10610 | any person to whom the right to any shares of the company has been
-- src:10611 | transmitted by operation of law.
@ref s 126(1) (src:10606-10611)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right to the shares has been transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126(1) the private company is barred from lodging the transfer of shares` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a private company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a private company must not lodge a transfer of shares" -- a scope limit with no "only"; the public company's rule is s 130(1)
    ELSE IF `the right to the shares has been transmitted to the person by operation of law`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section does not affect any power to lodge a notice of transfer of shares in respect of any person to whom the right to any shares of the company has been transmitted by operation of law"
         ELSE IF `a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not lodge a transfer of shares unless a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company" -- the bar is closed with "unless"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 126(1) (src:10606-10611)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 126 act`
`s 126(1) a private company must not lodge a transfer of shares without a proper instrument of transfer` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 126(1) lodge a transfer of shares without a proper instrument of transfer having been delivered to the company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company lodged a transfer of shares without a proper instrument of transfer having been delivered to it"

-- s 126(2): where there has been a transfer of shares, a private company must lodge with the Registrar notice of it in the prescribed form. No time is stated.
-- src:10615 | (2) Where there has been a transfer of shares, a private company
-- src:10616 | must lodge with the Registrar notice of that transfer of shares in the
-- src:10617 | prescribed form.
@ref s 126(2) (src:10615-10617)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a transfer of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126(2) the private company must lodge with the Registrar notice of the transfer of shares` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a private company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a private company must lodge" -- a scope limit with no "only"; the public company's rule is s 130(2)
    ELSE IF `there has been a transfer of shares`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, by item (b) of the periods ruling of 2026-11-05): "Where there has been a transfer of shares, a private company must lodge" -- a duty whose "where" is unmet: the duty does not arise (fork F-j126-1, as F-j83-1)

@ref s 126(2) (src:10615-10617)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 126 act`
`s 126(2) a private company must lodge notice of a transfer of shares with the Registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 126(2) lodge with the Registrar notice of the transfer of shares in the prescribed form`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 126(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company did not lodge with the Registrar notice of the transfer of shares in the prescribed form" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- s 126(3): a transfer on or after 3 January 2016 does not take effect until the electronic register of members is updated by the Registrar under s 196A(5) (ruling of 2026-11-05, item (d): encode the bar).
-- src:10624 | (3) A transfer of any share in a private company on or after
-- src:10625 | 3 January 2016 does not take effect until the electronic register of
-- src:10626 | members of the company is updated by the Registrar under
-- src:10627 | section 196A(5).
@ref s 126(3) (src:10624-10627)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126(3) the transfer cannot yet take effect` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` AND `the day of the transfer` AT LEAST `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN (IF `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not take effect until the electronic register of members of the company is updated" -- after the update the bar is lifted (ruling of 2026-11-05, item (d))
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A transfer of any share in a private company on or after 3 January 2016" -- a scope limit with no "only"

§ `Section 127: transfer of debentures in private companies`

DECLARE `s 127 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 127 register a transfer of debentures without a proper instrument of transfer having been delivered to the company`

-- src:10633 | 127. Despite anything in its constitution, a private company must
-- src:10634 | not register a transfer of debentures unless a proper instrument of
-- src:10635 | transfer has been delivered to the company, but this section does not
-- src:10636 | affect any power to register as debenture holder any person to whom
-- src:10637 | the right to any debentures of the company has been transmitted by
-- src:10638 | operation of law.
@ref s 127 (src:10633-10638)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the right to the debentures has been transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127 the private company is barred from registering the transfer of debentures` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a private company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a private company must not register a transfer of debentures" -- a scope limit with no "only"; the public company's rule is s 130(1)
    ELSE IF `the right to the debentures has been transmitted to the person by operation of law`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section does not affect any power to register as debenture holder any person to whom the right to any debentures of the company has been transmitted by operation of law"
         ELSE IF `a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not register a transfer of debentures unless a proper instrument of transfer has been delivered to the company" -- the bar is closed with "unless"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 127 (src:10633-10638)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 127 act`
`s 127 a private company must not register a transfer of debentures without a proper instrument of transfer` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 127 register a transfer of debentures without a proper instrument of transfer having been delivered to the company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company registered a transfer of debentures without a proper instrument of transfer having been delivered to it"

§ `Section 128: registration of transfer at request of transferor by private companies`

DECLARE `s 128 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 128(1)(a) lodge with the Registrar a notice of transfer of shares in the prescribed form`
    `s 128(1)(b) enter the name of the transferee in the register the company considers appropriate`
    `s 128(3) require by written notice the person having possession, custody or control to deliver or produce the share certificate or debenture and the instrument of transfer`
    `s 128(6) exhibit and advertise the list of share certificates or debentures called in and not delivered or produced`

-- s 128(1): subject to s 129, on the transferor's written request the company must lodge the notice of transfer (a share) or enter the transferee's name (a debenture or other interest).
-- src:10645 | 128.—(1) Subject to section 129, on the request in writing of the
-- src:10646 | transferor of —
-- src:10648 | (a) any share in a private company — the company must lodge
-- src:10649 | with the Registrar a notice of transfer of shares in the
-- src:10650 | prescribed form; or
-- src:10652 | (b) any debenture or other interest in a private company — the
-- src:10653 | company must enter in such register as the company
-- src:10654 | considers appropriate, the name of the transferee in the
-- src:10655 | same manner and subject to the same conditions as if the
-- src:10656 | application for the entry were made by the transferee.
@ref s 128(1) (src:10645-10656)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferor has made the request in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 129 allows the company to refuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128(1) the private company must act on the transferor's request` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` AND `the transferor has made the request in writing` AND (NOT `section 129 allows the company to refuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to section 129, on the request in writing of the transferor ... the company must" -- the duty is limited by the written request and by section 129; outside them the text is silent (fork F-j128-1)

@ref s 128(1) (src:10645-10656)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 128 act`
`s 128(1)(a) a private company must lodge a notice of transfer of shares on the transferor's request` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 128(1)(a) lodge with the Registrar a notice of transfer of shares in the prescribed form`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 128(1)(a) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company did not lodge with the Registrar a notice of transfer of shares on the written request of the transferor" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

@ref s 128(1) (src:10645-10656)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 128 act`
`s 128(1)(b) a private company must enter the name of the transferee on the transferor's request` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 128(1)(b) enter the name of the transferee in the register the company considers appropriate`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 128(1)(b) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company did not enter the name of the transferee on the written request of the transferor" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- s 128(2): as s 126(3).
-- src:10660 | (2) The transfer of any share in a private company on or after
-- src:10661 | 3 January 2016 does not take effect until the electronic register of
-- src:10662 | members of the company is updated by the Registrar under
-- src:10663 | section 196A(5).
@ref s 128(2) (src:10660-10663)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the transfer` IS A DATE
      `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128(2) the transfer cannot yet take effect` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` AND `the day of the transfer` AT LEAST `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN (IF `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not take effect until the electronic register of members of the company is updated" -- after the update the bar is lifted (ruling of 2026-11-05, item (d))
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The transfer of any share in a private company on or after 3 January 2016" -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- s 128(3): the notice requiring delivery within a stated period of not less than 7 and not more than 28 days after the date of the notice.
-- src:10667 | (3) On the request in writing of the transferor of a share or
-- src:10668 | debenture, the private company must by written notice require the
-- src:10669 | person having the possession, custody or control of the share
-- src:10670 | certificate or debenture and the instrument of transfer thereof or either
-- src:10675 | of them to deliver or produce it or them to the office of the company
-- src:10676 | within a stated period, being not less than 7 and not more than 28 days
-- src:10677 | after the date of the notice, to have the share certificate or debenture
-- src:10678 | cancelled or rectified, and the transfer registered (in the case of a
-- src:10679 | transfer of debenture) or otherwise dealt with.
@ref s 128(3) (src:10667-10679)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferor has made the request in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128(3) the private company must by written notice require delivery or production of the documents` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` AND `the transferor has made the request in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the request in writing of the transferor of a share or debenture, the private company must" -- without the written request, or for another company, the text is silent

@ref s 128(3) (src:10667-10679)
GIVEN `the number of days after the date of the notice that the notice states` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128(3) the period stated in the notice is a period the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the number of days after the date of the notice that the notice states` AT LEAST 7 AND `the number of days after the date of the notice that the notice states` AT MOST 28
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within a stated period, being not less than 7 and not more than 28 days after the date of the notice"

@ref s 128(3) (src:10667-10679)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 128 act`
`s 128(3) a private company must require delivery or production of the documents by written notice` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 128(3) require by written notice the person having possession, custody or control to deliver or produce the share certificate or debenture and the instrument of transfer`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 128(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company did not require by written notice the person having possession, custody or control to deliver or produce the documents" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- s 128(4): if a person refuses or neglects to comply with the notice, the transferor may apply to a judge for a summons. A grant gated by "if": NOTHING (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-j128-2).
-- src:10683 | (4) If any person refuses or neglects to comply with a notice given
-- src:10684 | under subsection (3), the transferor may apply to a judge to issue a
-- src:10685 | summons for that person to appear before the Court and show cause
-- src:10686 | why the documents mentioned in the notice should not be delivered or
-- src:10687 | produced as required by the notice.
@ref s 128(4) (src:10683-10687)
GIVEN `the person has refused or neglected to comply with a notice given under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128(4) the transferor may apply to a judge for a summons` MEANS
    IF `the person has refused or neglected to comply with a notice given under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If any person refuses or neglects to comply with a notice given under subsection (3), the transferor may apply to a judge" -- a grant whose "if" gate is unmet

-- s 128(5): upon the appearance of the person summoned (or, if the person does not appear after being duly served, in the person's absence) the Court may order delivery of the documents to the company.
-- A "may" gated by "upon": answered as item (b) of the periods ruling of 2026-11-05 gives it (JUST FALSE), "upon" counting as "where" under item (c) of the delegated-definitions ruling of the same date, and listed for a lawyer (fork F-j128-3, split site (ii)).
-- src:10691 | (5) Upon appearance of a person so summoned the Court may
-- src:10692 | examine the person upon oath and receive other evidence, or if the
-- src:10693 | person does not appear after being duly served with such summons,
-- src:10694 | the Court may receive evidence in the person’s absence and in either
-- src:10695 | case the Court may order the person to deliver such documents to the
-- src:10696 | company upon such terms or conditions as to the Court seem fit, and
-- src:10697 | the costs of the summons and proceedings thereon are in the
-- src:10698 | discretion of the Court.
@ref s 128(5) (src:10691-10698)
GIVEN `the person has been summoned under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has appeared` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has not appeared after being duly served with the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128(5) the Court may order the person to deliver the documents to the company` MEANS
    IF `the person has been summoned under subsection (4)` AND (`the person has appeared` OR `the person has not appeared after being duly served with the summons`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, by item (b) of the periods ruling and item (c) of the delegated-definitions ruling, both of 2026-11-05): "Upon appearance of a person so summoned ... or if the person does not appear after being duly served ..., the Court may order the person to deliver such documents" -- a "may" gated by "upon" (listed for a lawyer)

-- s 128(6): the lists of share certificates or debentures called in and not delivered must be exhibited in the company's office and advertised. No time is stated.
-- src:10702 | (6) Lists of share certificates or debentures called in under this
