-- src:10704 | of the company and must be advertised in such newspapers and at
-- src:10705 | such times as the company thinks fit.
@ref s 128(6) (src:10702-10705)
GIVEN `share certificates or debentures have been called in under section 128 and have not been delivered or produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128(6) the company must exhibit the list in its office and advertise it` MEANS
    IF `share certificates or debentures have been called in under section 128 and have not been delivered or produced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Lists of share certificates or debentures called in under this section and not delivered or produced"

@ref s 128(6) (src:10702-10705)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 128 act`
`s 128(6) the company must exhibit and advertise the list` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 128(6) exhibit and advertise the list of share certificates or debentures called in and not delivered or produced`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 128(6) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not exhibit in its office and advertise the list of share certificates or debentures called in and not delivered or produced" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

§ `Section 128A: repealed by Act 36 of 2014`

-- src:10709 | 128A. [Repealed by Act 36 of 2014]

§ `Section 129: notice of refusal to register transfer by private companies`

DECLARE `s 129 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 129(1) send to the transferor and the transferee notice of the refusal to lodge a notice of transfer of a share`
    `s 129(2) send to the transferor and the transferee notice of the refusal to register a transfer of a debenture or other interest`
    `s 129(3) refuse to lodge a notice of transfer by virtue of a discretion in the constitution`

-- s 129(1): within 30 days after the date on which the transfer was lodged with the company (the day of lodging is not counted: sg-periods P1).
-- src:10713 | 129.—(1) If a private company refuses to lodge a notice of transfer
-- src:10714 | of any share in the company it must, within 30 days after the date on
-- src:10715 | which the transfer was lodged with it, send to the transferor and the
-- src:10716 | transferee notice of the refusal.
@ref s 129(1) (src:10713-10716)
GIVEN `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 129(1) the last day for sending notice of the refusal` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` 30 Days

@ref s 129(1) (src:10713-10716)
GIVEN `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice of the refusal was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(1) the notice of the refusal was sent within 30 days` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice of the refusal was sent` AT MOST (`s 129(1) the last day for sending notice of the refusal` `the day the transfer was lodged with the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must, within 30 days after the date on which the transfer was lodged with it, send to the transferor and the transferee notice of the refusal" -- a period the text fixes in its own words

@ref s 129(1) (src:10713-10716)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 129 act`
`s 129(1) a private company that refuses to lodge a notice of transfer must send notice of the refusal within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 129(1) send to the transferor and the transferee notice of the refusal to lodge a notice of transfer of a share`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company did not send to the transferor and the transferee notice of the refusal within 30 days after the date on which the transfer was lodged"

-- s 129(2): the same for a refusal to register a transfer of a debenture or other interest.
