-- src:10721 | debenture or other interest in the company it must, within 30 days
-- src:10726 | after the date on which the transfer was lodged with it, send to the
-- src:10727 | transferor and to the transferee notice of the refusal.
@ref s 129(2) (src:10720-10727)
GIVEN `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 129(2) the last day for sending notice of the refusal` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` 30 Days

@ref s 129(2) (src:10720-10727)
GIVEN `the day the transfer was lodged with the company` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice of the refusal was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(2) the notice of the refusal was sent within 30 days` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice of the refusal was sent` AT MOST (`s 129(2) the last day for sending notice of the refusal` `the day the transfer was lodged with the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must, within 30 days after the date on which the transfer was lodged with it, send to the transferor and to the transferee notice of the refusal" -- a period the text fixes in its own words

@ref s 129(2) (src:10720-10727)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 129 act`
`s 129(2) a private company that refuses to register a transfer must send notice of the refusal within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 129(2) send to the transferor and the transferee notice of the refusal to register a transfer of a debenture or other interest`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company did not send to the transferor and the transferee notice of the refusal within 30 days after the date on which the transfer was lodged"

-- s 129(3): the company must not refuse by virtue of a discretion in the constitution unless it has served a written notice of the facts within 30 days beginning with the day the application was made (sg-periods P10).
-- src:10731 | (3) Where an application is made to a private company to lodge
-- src:10732 | with the Registrar a notice of transfer in the prescribed form in respect
-- src:10733 | of any share that has been transferred or transmitted to a person by act
-- src:10734 | of parties or operation of law, the company must not refuse to do so by
-- src:10735 | virtue of any discretion in that behalf conferred by the constitution
-- src:10736 | unless it has served on the applicant, within 30 days beginning with
-- src:10737 | the day on which the application was made, a written notice stating
-- src:10738 | the facts which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that
-- src:10739 | discretion.
@ref s 129(3) (src:10731-10739)
GIVEN `the day the application was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 129(3) the last day for serving the written notice` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period beginning with` `the day the application was made` 30 Days

@ref s 129(3) (src:10731-10739)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application relates to a share that has been transferred or transmitted to a person by act of parties or operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal was served on the applicant` IS A DATE
      `a written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that discretion has been served on the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(3) the private company is barred from refusing by virtue of a discretion in the constitution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`) OR (NOT `the application relates to a share that has been transferred or transmitted to a person by act of parties or operation of law`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an application is made to a private company ... in respect of any share that has been transferred or transmitted to a person by act of parties or operation of law" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE IF `a written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal in the exercise of that discretion has been served on the applicant`
              AND (`the day the written notice stating the facts which are considered to justify refusal was served on the applicant` AT MOST (`s 129(3) the last day for serving the written notice` `the day the application was made`))
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not refuse ... unless it has served on the applicant, within 30 days beginning with the day on which the application was made, a written notice stating the facts" -- the bar is closed with "unless"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 129(3) as a regulative rule: the prohibition is on refusing without the notice. The act carries whether the notice was served in time; refusing with no timely notice is BREACH.
DECLARE `s 129(3) refusal` IS ONE OF
    `s 129(3) refusal by virtue of a discretion` HAS `the written notice was served on the applicant within 30 days beginning with the day the application was made` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 129(3) (src:10731-10739)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 129(3) refusal`
`s 129(3) a private company must not refuse by virtue of a discretion without a timely written notice` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 129(3) refusal by virtue of a discretion` served PROVIDED NOT served
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the private company refused to lodge the notice of transfer by virtue of a discretion in the constitution without having served a written notice stating the facts within 30 days beginning with the day of the application"

-- s 129(4): the offence of default.
-- src:10745 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section, the private
-- src:10746 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall
-- src:10747 | each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a
-- src:10748 | fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 129(4) (src:10745-10748)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 129` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 129` AND (`the person is the private company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, the private company and every officer of the company who is in default shall each be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet (split site (i), fork line F-j129-1)

@ref s 129(4) (src:10745-10748)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 129` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 129(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 129(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 129` `the person is the private company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    --                          fine, months, both, default penalty
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty
